From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 16:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mfd: mt6358: Fix AUD and MISC top interrupt status bits

In TOP_INT_STATUS0 the MT6358 and MT6366 report the AUD group at bit 7
and the MISC group at bit 8. Bit 6 is unused. MediaTek's downstream
headers say so (MT6358_AUD_TOP = 7). The mainline enum gives them 6 and
7, so mt6358_irq_handler() takes a pending AUD interrupt for MISC. It
reads an empty MISC status, does not dispatch or acknowledge the AUD
source, and the level-triggered PMIC line fires again at once.

On an MT6366 (Zinwa Q25), enabling ACCDET_EINT0 with a headset plugged
in left TOP_INT_STATUS0 at 0x0080 and AUD_TOP_INT_STATUS0 at 0x0040,
with MISC_TOP_INT_STATUS0 at 0. The PMIC interrupt then ran at about
24000/s while the ACCDET handlers never ran.
---
 include/linux/mfd/mt6358/core.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/linux/mfd/mt6358/core.h b/include/linux/mfd/mt6358/core.h
--- a/include/linux/mfd/mt6358/core.h
+++ b/include/linux/mfd/mt6358/core.h
@@ -32,7 +32,7 @@
 	MT6358_SCK_TOP,
 	MT6358_BM_TOP,
 	MT6358_HK_TOP,
-	MT6358_AUD_TOP,
+	MT6358_AUD_TOP = 7,
 	MT6358_MISC_TOP,
 };
 
